{"id": "EUVD-2025-208821", "enisaUuid": "3c6ca8af-433c-3796-94a2-c52c6293ce24", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs: ntfs3: fix infinite loop triggered by zero-sized ATTR_LIST\n\nWe found an infinite loop bug in the ntfs3 file system that can lead to a\nDenial-of-Service (DoS) condition.\n\nA malformed NTFS image can cause an infinite loop when an ATTR_LIST attribute\nindicates a zero data size while the driver allocates memory for it.\n\nWhen ntfs_load_attr_list() processes a resident ATTR_LIST with data_size set\nto zero, it still allocates memory because of al_aligned(0). This creates an\ninconsistent state where ni->attr_list.size is zero, but ni->attr_list.le is\nnon-null. This causes ni_enum_attr_ex to incorrectly assume that no attribute\nlist exists and enumerates only the primary MFT record. When it finds\nATTR_LIST, the code reloads it and restarts the enumeration, repeating\nindefinitely. The mount operation never completes, hanging the kernel thread.\n\nThis patch adds validation to ensure that data_size is non-zero before memory\nallocation. When a zero-sized ATTR_LIST is detected, the function returns\n-EINVAL, preventing a DoS vulnerability.", "datePublished": "2026-03-18T10:05:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:11:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9267d99fade76d44d4a133599524031fe684156e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/976e6a7c51fabf150478decbe8ef5d9a26039b7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d8c70b57dbeda3eb165c0940b97e85373ca9354", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ef219656febf5ae06ae56b1fce47ebd05f92b68", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9779a6eaaabdf47aa57910d352b398ad742e6a5f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd508939dbca5eceefb2d0c2564beb15469572f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06909b2549d631a47fcda249d34be26f7ca1711d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-71267", "GHSA-j72w-3754-92gg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07079d42-6169-3753-a004-f738efd6684e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be71b5cba2e6485e8959da7a9f9a44461a1bb074 <9267d99fade76d44d4a133599524031fe684156e"}, {"id": "0acb1b1d-8d1f-3410-9696-e1391357b47c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.16"}, {"id": "0b223c83-38dd-31df-bbc4-b72e91d0458b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.128"}, {"id": "2231b9f4-1894-34f5-80f2-7ad4569cc7d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be71b5cba2e6485e8959da7a9f9a44461a1bb074 <fd508939dbca5eceefb2d0c2564beb15469572f2"}, {"id": "45a21ad3-c999-3d03-b490-162024f59b9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be71b5cba2e6485e8959da7a9f9a44461a1bb074 <976e6a7c51fabf150478decbe8ef5d9a26039b7c"}, {"id": "5496e22b-177d-3646-b83f-4d9a34d4b86f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "55c9f5a8-f38e-312d-9cc3-97479c43dfac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be71b5cba2e6485e8959da7a9f9a44461a1bb074 <8d8c70b57dbeda3eb165c0940b97e85373ca9354"}, {"id": "72d31eb2-e9c0-3f16-87e6-d10a541e9d95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "86413637-6000-3939-ab52-aafc2c7d3196", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "913c27a4-1ed9-3553-8ae4-10238d859785", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "9153c04b-f9f7-39bf-8fe1-22444175de26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be71b5cba2e6485e8959da7a9f9a44461a1bb074 <06909b2549d631a47fcda249d34be26f7ca1711d"}, {"id": "9f2e3ae9-bb1e-3548-a8ae-7a156c36e0f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be71b5cba2e6485e8959da7a9f9a44461a1bb074 <9779a6eaaabdf47aa57910d352b398ad742e6a5f"}, {"id": "a556af71-e04f-3d27-bb6c-5c7b1cab50c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be71b5cba2e6485e8959da7a9f9a44461a1bb074 <7ef219656febf5ae06ae56b1fce47ebd05f92b68"}, {"id": "a6f4f8f5-5201-331c-a6c0-524c113be614", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.165"}, {"id": "aecf7f0f-d801-34c3-a3c5-994b68316f6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.202"}, {"id": "c78e0c9e-0d1a-3060-b107-4c78f08ac003", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.75"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "34fe4a37-ff96-325f-99a8-73d5a06eb8e5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}